# Shell scripts and Python MUST be LF, whatever the checkout platform.
#
# A CRLF shebang becomes `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`, the kernel looks for an
# interpreter literally named "bash\r", and systemd reports 203/EXEC — a failure
# that names neither the file nor the reason. This repo is edited on Windows and
# run on a Jetson, so that path is live rather than theoretical.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.rules text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
